\series medium
\shape up
\size normal
\emph off
\bar no
\strikeout off
\uuline off
\uwave off
\noun off
\color none

\begin_inset Formula $p^{*}\rightarrow c$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
Q^{*}(p^{*})={\displaystyle \sum_{i=1}^{I}}(\alpha-\beta p^{*})=I(\alpha-\beta p^{*})
\]

\end_inset


\family default
\series default
\shape default
\size default
\emph default
\bar default
\strikeout default
\uuline default
\uwave default
\noun default
\color inherit
At equilibrium, quantity demanded equals quantity supplied, so we can easily
 derive what happens to equilibrium quantity as 
\begin_inset Formula $I\rightarrow\infty$
\end_inset

 by analyzing aggregate quantity demand as a function of price.
 It was already determined that 
